            {
                "entry_id": "58600792-3d77-3fe0-b269-902ae4969916",
                "word": "ree",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "02e8708a-82ca-4d44-8f7e-643027c369de",
                        "entry_id": "58600792-3d77-3fe0-b269-902ae4969916",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "rees"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c31f658e-7d60-36fa-b2ec-ea54e9c097be",
                        "entry_id": "58600792-3d77-3fe0-b269-902ae4969916",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A period of stormy or unsettled weather, especially one occurring somewhat predictably at a particular time of year."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland",
                            "Shetland",
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "30f05196-0067-4cc0-830a-f74d34930b50",
                                "sense_id": "c31f658e-7d60-36fa-b2ec-ea54e9c097be",
                                "text": "To my surprise he took our caustic remarks about the climate very calmly, even cheerfully. \"Och, man, it's only the Beltane ree,\" he said with a lively twinkle, enjoying our bewilderment. Evidently, the Shetland weather was merely putting on a scheduled performance and he for one was very well satisfied with its achievement - but the Beltane ree . . . ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e64eb29-8abe-4f09-94ea-28a9cdd70bfe",
                                "sense_id": "c31f658e-7d60-36fa-b2ec-ea54e9c097be",
                                "text": "There were three \"Rees\" (wild tempests), Buggle Ree, Beltane Ree, and Simmer-mill Ree."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90e27367-992b-46b3-8041-6e0b206eaca6",
                                "sense_id": "c31f658e-7d60-36fa-b2ec-ea54e9c097be",
                                "text": "[…] rees. There were four rees in the first half of the year – the Bogel ree in March, the Simmermill ree in April, the Beltane ree about the beginning of May, and the Johnsmas ree which brought a short spell of unsettled weather in the latter half of June."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "0bf64630-0d7b-3747-8573-7bd6a9d1ba06",
                "word": "REE",
